                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6987: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-31T17:00:00+08:00">May 31, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 31—1:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>133. I hear from an official source that the Japanese demonstration yesterday
                    before the Provincial Government headquarters in Tientsin <pb facs="0304"
                        n="192" xml:id="pg192"/> was accompanied by “advice” that the Provincial
                    Government move to Paotingfu without delay, that similar warning has been given
                    Ho Ying-chin in respect to the Peiping Military Affairs Council, and that both
                    Yu Hsueh-chung and Ho are taking steps to comply.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
